@startuml documents
title Documents: reads, edits, recovery and subscriptions
autonumber
actor "User" as User
participant "CLI / TUI\nPresentation" as Client
participant "CLI internal/app" as ClientApp
participant "Document client\nHTTP OR gRPC adapter" as Remote
box "hermes-document-service" #E0F4E0
participant "API + session middleware" as API
participant "internal/app" as App
participant "internal/domain\nPolicies / invariants" as Domain
participant "internal/postgres\nUnitOfWork / repositories" as Repo
end box
database "Document PostgreSQL" as DB
note over Remote, App
  Protected requests follow auth.puml: middleware -> Auth -> Redis SessionStore.
  Only a valid session reaches the use case; Redis failure returns unavailable.
  App receives authenticated identity, never a client-supplied actor ID.
  Domain access checks use current data through repositories.
end note
note over App, DB
  Mutations use one PostgreSQL transaction with current access and version checks.
  Any failed check rolls back all writes; unchanged state creates no change event.
  Domain facts from committed changes follow events_dispatch.puml.
  Outbox/CDC versus direct publication remains OPEN (ADR-002).
end note

== Create document ==
User -> Client : Create document(workspace, title, Markdown)
Client -> ClientApp : Documents.Create
ClientApp -> Remote : CreateDocument
Remote -> API : Protected request
API -> App : Documents.Create(actor, request)
App -> Repo : Transaction: load workspace and actor membership
Repo -> DB : BEGIN; read current state
App -> Domain : Require active workspace, editor/admin/owner and non-empty title
App -> Repo : Create document(version=1, author=actor)
Repo -> DB : INSERT; COMMIT / ROLLBACK
App --> API : Document/version + DocumentCreated fact after commit / error
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Result
ClientApp --> Client : Result
note over App
  Personal documents belong to personal workspace.
  Live workspace update and personal notification are distinct policies.
  DocumentCreated recipients are OPEN; no blanket personal inbox fan-out.
end note

== List, search and read ==
ClientApp -> Remote : ListDocuments / SearchDocuments / GetDocument
Remote -> API : Protected query
API -> App : Documents query(actor, filters, cursor / id)
App -> Repo : Access-filtered read of active documents in active workspaces
Repo -> DB : SELECT with current membership and pagination predicate
DB --> Repo : Page / document / unavailable
Repo --> App : Result
App --> API : DTO data; reads create no events
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Application models / errors
ClientApp --> Client : Show results / plain Markdown for CLI read

== Begin edit and launch editor ==
User -> Client : Edit document
Client -> ClientApp : Documents.BeginEdit(document_id)
ClientApp -> Remote : GetDocument(id)
Remote -> API : Protected read
API -> App : Documents.Get(actor, id)
App -> Repo : Read document with current access predicate
Repo -> DB : SELECT
Repo --> App : Accessible document + version / error
App --> API : Result
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Document / error
alt Accessible document and local draft persisted
  ClientApp -> ClientApp : DraftStore.Create(base snapshot, version, working file, server/user)
  ClientApp --> Client : Draft with persistent working path
  Client -> Client : Suspend TUI; SystemEditor.Edit(path); resume terminal
  User -> Client : Finish or cancel editor
else Read or local storage failed
  ClientApp --> Client : Error; do not launch editor
end
note over Client, ClientApp
  Editor changes the existing local draft only; it does not upload or delete it.
  Cancellation/editor failure preserves the draft. Live transport is independent
  of terminal rendering; reconnect/gap recovery follows notifications_inbox.puml.
end note

== Save edited document ==
Client -> ClientApp : Documents.SaveEdit(draft_id)
ClientApp -> ClientApp : Load draft; check server/account; read working file
ClientApp -> Remote : UpdateDocument(id, title, content, BaseVersion)
Remote -> API : Protected mutation
API -> App : Documents.Update(actor, request)
App -> Repo : Transaction: load active document/workspace, membership and version
Repo -> DB : BEGIN; read/lock current state
App -> Domain : Check edit role, expected_version and content changes
alt Permission lost / unavailable / version mismatch
  App -> Repo : Roll back
  Repo -> DB : ROLLBACK
  App --> API : Access error / conflict
else Matching version and unchanged content
  Repo -> DB : COMMIT without writes
  App --> API : Current document; no event
else Valid changed content
  App -> Repo : Persist title/content; increment version and attribution
  Repo -> DB : UPDATE; COMMIT / ROLLBACK on persistence failure
  App --> API : Saved document + DocumentUpdated fact after commit / error
end
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : saved / unchanged / conflict / failed / unknown
alt Confirmed saved or unchanged
  ClientApp -> ClientApp : DraftStore.Delete; report cleanup failure separately
  ClientApp --> Client : Save result
else Conflict, lost access, network failure or unknown outcome
  ClientApp --> Client : Keep draft; show recovery path and outcome
  opt User requests comparison and still has read access
    Client -> ClientApp : Documents.CompareLatest(draft_id)
    ClientApp -> Remote : GetDocument via same protected read path
    Remote --> ClientApp : Latest accessible snapshot / error
    ClientApp --> Client : Base + local + latest for manual review
    User -> Client : Review / merge and explicitly choose reviewed base
    Client -> ClientApp : Documents.RebaseDraft(draft_id, reviewedVersion)
    ClientApp -> ClientApp : Update base snapshot/version; preserve working content
  end
end
note over ClientApp
  No automatic overwrite, merge or blind mutation retry.
  Unknown save outcome requires inspecting current document; a read alone
  does not prove which operation produced identical content.
  Another writer may cause a new conflict on the next SaveEdit.
end note

== Subscribe / unsubscribe ==
ClientApp -> Remote : SubscribeDocument / UnsubscribeDocument
Remote -> API : Protected request
API -> App : Documents subscription use case(actor, id)
App -> Repo : Transaction: read active target and membership
Repo -> DB : BEGIN; SELECT current state
App -> Domain : Require read access; subscription grants no permission
App -> Repo : Change subscription only when state differs
Repo -> DB : INSERT / DELETE; COMMIT / ROLLBACK
App --> API : Current state; SubscriptionCreated/Deleted only on committed change
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Result

== Delete document ==
User -> Client : Confirm deletion of a previously read version
Client -> ClientApp : Documents.Delete(id, expected_version, confirmation)
ClientApp -> Remote : DeleteDocument
Remote -> API : Protected request
API -> App : Documents.Delete(actor, request)
App -> Repo : Transaction: read/lock target and current membership
Repo -> DB : BEGIN
App -> Domain : Require editor/admin/owner, active target, version and confirmation
App -> Repo : Capture subscriber IDs; soft-delete document; remove subscriptions
Repo -> DB : COMMIT valid changes / ROLLBACK
App --> API : Result; DocumentDeleted fact after commit
API --> Remote : Result
Remote --> ClientApp : Result
note over App, DB
  A minimal deletion notice may be routed to eligible subscribers.
  Opening a deleted target returns unavailable; old notices grant no access.
end note
@enduml
